  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the system of linear equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> be the set of all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> for which the system is inconsistent and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> be the set of all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> for which the system has infinitely many solutions. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math> denote the number of elements in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> respectively, then</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For system to be inconsistent&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>7</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>31</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext>&#160;for&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Similarly we can show&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext>&#160;for&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now for infinitely many solutions&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>also&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;which is not possible value of any real of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>, since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;have different solutions for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>"
  }
